9	//   - The same logs with the same network must produce byte-for-byte the
10	//     same records, in the same order, with the same physical line numbers
11	//     and the same failure count, whether the input arrives as one piece,
12	//     one byte at a time, or alternating short and long chunks.
13	//   - Membership is decided on the fully normalized source_ip: 192.0.2.7 and
14	//     ::ffff:192.0.2.7 admit identically (also via the src_ip alias, and a
15	//     canonical name plus an alias spelling of the same address merge into
16	//     one success record), while ::192.0.2.7 stays IPv6 — valid but dropped.
17	//     Out-of-network and source-less valid logs are dropped without
18	//     failing, and dropped or blank lines never renumber later records.
19	//   - The filter never hides bad logs and never rewrites hits: a failed
20	//     line keeps its physical number and original reason, and admitted
21	//     records are exactly the records the unfiltered run would emit.
22	//   - A partial delivery (a read fault with an unterminated fragment)
23	//     must not turn the fragment into an extra record or an extra failure.
